# ChakraOps Cursor Rules

## Scope

- Implement approved scope only.
- Stop if scope expands beyond what the operator explicitly authorized.
- Master program R36.3–R40 authorizes continuous acceptance-loop work on `main`.

## Git

- Default: `SINGLE_OPERATOR_MAINLINE_LOOP_MODE` per `AGENTS.md`.
- Commit/push on `main` only after the current release acceptance contract is green, when the operator (or master program) authorized it.
- Never force-push or rewrite history.
- Keep `chakraOpsDropbox/` untracked (local exclude).

## Protected Paths

- Do not modify files under `out/` or `data/` except authorized verification evidence under `out/verification/<Release>/`.
- Do not modify past release notes (any release prior to the current release).

## Trading Safety

- Preserve manual-only execution. Do not add or imply automated order routing.
- Preserve ORATS-only provider rule. Do not add silent provider fallbacks.
- Preserve safe UI labels. Do not expose raw `FAIL_`, `WARN_`, or `PASS` tokens in UI-facing output.
- Scheduler remains disabled unless the operator explicitly enables it.
- Robinhood integration, if any, is hard read-only with write denylist.

## Required Gates Before DONE

1. Backend: `cd chakraops && python -m pytest tests -q --tb=short`
2. Frontend tests: `cd frontend && npm run test -- --run`
3. Frontend build: `cd frontend && npm run build`

## Continuous Acceptance

inspect → implement → targeted test → runtime/browser validate → compare to requirements → fix → repeat

## STEP Report Format

At major release boundaries only, provide a concise progress summary:

- **Files changed** — list every file created or modified
- **Tests run** — exact command and summary line
- **Exact summaries** — paste the final summary lines from each gate
- **Skipped items** — what was deferred and why
- **Open risks** — anything that may require follow-up
- **Stop point** — only when a genuine blocker remains; otherwise continue to the next release
